-- Native world kinds, entity half (s53a), ASCII twin: kanji columns in num/bool/sym, a presence mask behind 両手 (junk decoys per ex06), a functional rel with its inverse srel, an explicit srel, entity/mask/num bindings, and a kanji-named reducer — every emission site of the name mangler on one world. (was s53-native-kinds-a)
-- A guild born in kanji: masters, disciples, factions. Every entity-world registry kind on one fixture, so a mangler regression has nowhere to hide.
-- Statement walk: pres+bind-num masked add; gamma count over the inverse fiber under a sym predicate; rel hop into the sym column; mask binding AND col with a gamma over the explicit srel; then two queries — the kanji reducer and an entity-binding mirror-read.
--! registry ../registries/098-native-kinds-a.reg
--! out 600
--! out 300
--! expect 金 = 160 200 300 460 500 600
--! expect 打撃 = 2 2 0 0 1 0
--! expect 派閥 = Bandit Player Bandit Nord Nord Nord
--! expect-n 6

北 & 両手 > 60 , 金 += 補給
派閥 == :Nord , 打撃 += #/ 弟子団'
師匠.派閥 == :Bandit , 金 += 10
城内 & 北 , 打撃 += #/ 標的'
fold(脅威) 金 @ 北
主人公.金
